  'bronkhorstspruit-plant-repairs-nearing-final-stage-2026-10-28',
  'Tshwane says Bronkhorstspruit plant repairs nearing final stage',
  'Utilities', '2026-10-28', 'TimesLIVE', 'https://www.timeslive.co.za/politics/2026-10-28-city-of-tshwane-reports-progress-in-bronkhorstspruit-water-repairs/',
  'The City of Tshwane says repair work at the Bronkhorstspruit water treatment works is close to finishing its cleaning stage, but the unsafe water advisory for the area stays in force.',
  'The City of Tshwane says work to fix the Bronkhorstspruit water treatment works is approaching a key milestone. The municipality reported that the biggest of the plant''s two reservoirs has now been fully cleaned, while the second, smaller reservoir still needs extra equipment to remove built-up sludge before its own clean-up can be finished. Getting the filtration system ready for use was about 90% done, including checks on its electrical parts, and a generator has been connected at the point where raw water is drawn from the river while the remaining electrical wiring is completed.

Once the reservoir cleaning is done, the next steps are circulating water through the system internally, adding chlorine and flushing the network, before the plant can be tested and brought back into service. For now, the advisory telling residents supplied by the Bronkhorstspruit works, and the Hammanskraal phase 3 network, not to drink or cook with their tap water remains in place, and the city has not given a date for when it expects to lift it. Officials have also repeated earlier advice that putting this water through a boil first will not remove the risk, and that any of it kept in containers from before the advisory started should be poured away rather than used.

Separately, the city said it found higher-than-normal turbidity, a measure of how cloudy water is, at a water tanker filling point in Cullinan on the Tuesday before this update. Tanker filling at that point was suspended while the city brought in Magalies Water to help investigate, and officials were waiting on water test results before deciding when filling there could resume.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.timeslive.co.za/politics/2026-10-28-city-of-tshwane-reports-progress-in-bronkhorstspruit-water-repairs/", "https://www.enca.com/news-top-stories/bronkhorstspruit-reservoir-cleaning-near-completion", "https://www.sanews.gov.za/node/85236"]',
  'agent'
);
